<main id="content"><header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Umicom Framework &amp; Applications</p><h1>Find a Framework interface</h1><p class="lead">Locate public headers without searching thousands of unrelated files.</p></header>
<p>This catalogue is generated from public headers in the current Framework checkout. Search a component name or path, then open the header. Directories are source families, not proof of a complete runtime module or platform implementation.</p><p class="compact">Source links use reference <code>@UMICOM_SITE_SOURCE_REF@</code>. Inventory: <strong>@UMICOM_SITE_HEADER_COUNT@ headers</strong> in <strong>@UMICOM_SITE_FAMILY_COUNT@ source families</strong>. See the <a href="wiki/index.html">worked topics</a> for usage and the <a href="reference/html/index.html">optional generated API reference</a> for functions and types.</p><label for="source-search">Find a public header</label><input id="source-search" type="search" placeholder="For example: document, build, component, trading" aria-describedby="filter-help"><p id="filter-help" class="compact">The filter runs locally in your browser. Without JavaScript, all entries remain visible.</p><p id="source-count" role="status" aria-live="polite">@UMICOM_SITE_HEADER_COUNT@ header entries</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Source family</th><th>Public header</th></tr></thead><tbody>@UMICOM_SITE_HEADER_ROWS@</tbody></table></div>
</main><footer><strong>Umicom Foundation</strong><p>Learn from the source. Build with shared components.</p><a href="contributing.html">Improve these guides</a> · <a href="https://github.com/umicom-foundation">GitHub organisation</a></footer></body></html>
